hadiths[64]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4985","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] was asked: ""Which deed is best?"" ""He said: Faith in Allah [SWT] and His messenger [SAW]"
"4986","It was narrated from Abdullah bin Hubshi Al-Khath'ami that:The Prophet [SAW] was asked: ""Which deed is best?"" He said: ""Faith in which there is no doubt"
"4987","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""The messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'There are three things"
"4988","It was narrated that Qatadah said:""I heard Anas bin Malik narrating that the Prophet [SAW] said: 'There are three things"
"4989","It was narrated from Anas that :The Prophet [SAW] said: ""There are three things"
"4990","Abdullah bin 'Umar said:""Umar bin Al-Khattab told me: 'While we were with the Messenger of Allah [SAW] one day"
"4991","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah and Abu Dharr said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] would sit among his Companions and if a stranger came"
"4992","It was narrated from 'Amir bin Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas that his father said:""The Prophet [SAW] gave a share (of some spoils of war) to some men and not to others. Sa'd said: 'O Messenger of Allah [SAW]"
"4993","It was narrated from Sa'd that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] distributed (some spoils of war) and gave to some people but withheld from others. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah"
"4994","It was narrated from Bishr bin Suhaim that:The Prophet [SAW] commanded him to call out on the days of At-Tashriq that no one would enter Paradise except a believer"
"4995","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the people are safe"
"4996","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: ""The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe"
"4997","It was narrated that Anas said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever prays as we pray"
"4998","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'If a person accepts Islam"
"4999","It was narrated that Abu Musa said:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"5000","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr that:A man asked the Messenger of Allah [SAW]: ""What quality of Islam is best?"" He said: ""To feed (the poor) and to say the Salam to whomever one knows and whomever one does not know"
"5001","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:A man said to him: ""Why don't you go out and fight?"" He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'Islam is built on five (pillars): Testimony that there is none worthy of worship except Allah"
"5002","It was narrated that 'Ubadah bin As-Samit said:""We were with the Prophet [SAW] in a gathering and he said: 'Give me your pledge that you will not associate anything with Allah"
"5003","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness that there is none worthy of worship except Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. If they bear witness that there is none worthy of worship except Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah"
"5004","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Faith has seventy odd branches and modesty (Al-Haya') is a branch of faith"
"5005","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Faith has seventy-odd branches"
"5006","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Modesty (Al-Haya') is a branch of Faith"
"5007","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shurahbil"
"5008","Abu Sa'eed said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'Whoever among you sees an evil"
"5009","It was narrated that Tariq bin Shihab said:""Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: Whoever among you sees an evil and changes it with his hand"
"5010","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'No one of you disputes more intensely for something that is rightly his in this world"
"5011","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'While I was sleeping"
"5012","It was narrated that Tariq bin Shihab said:""A Jewish man came to 'Umar bin Al-Khattab and said: 'O Commander of the Believers! There is a Verse in your Book which you recite; if it had been revealed to us Jews we would have taken that day as a festival.' He said: 'Which Verse is that?' He said: 'This day"
"5013","It was narrated from Qatadah that:He heard Anas say: ""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'None of you has believed until I am dearer to him than his son"
"5014","It was narrated that Anas said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'None of you has believed until I am dearer to him than his family"
"5015","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""By the One in Whose hand is my soul"
"5016","It was narrated that Qatadah said:""I heard Anas say: 'The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said (Humaid bin Mas'dah said in his Hadith: 'The Prophet of Allah [SAW] said): None of you has believed until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself"
"5017","It was narrated from Anas that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad"
"5018","It was narrated that Zirr said:'Ali said: ""The Unlettered Prophet [SAW] made a covenant with me"
"5019","It was narrated from Anas that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Love for Ansar is a sign of Faith"
"5020","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""There are four (traits)"
"5021","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""The signs of the hypocrite are three: When he speaks"
"5022","It was narrated that 'Ali said:""The Prophet [SAW] made a covenant with me that none would love me but a believer"
"5023","It was narrated that Abu Wa'il said:""Abdullah said: 'There are three (traits)"
"5024","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""Whoever stands (in he voluntary night prayer of) the Ramadan out of faith and in the hope of reward"
"5025","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that :The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Whoever stands (in the voluntary night prayer of) Ramadan out of faith and in hope of reward"
"5026","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Whoever stands (in the voluntary night prayer of) Ramadan out of faith and in the hope of reward"
"5027","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""Whoever stands (in the voluntary night prayer of) Ramadan out of faith and in the hope of reward"
"5028","Abu Suhail narrated from his father"
"5029","Abu Hurairah said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'Allah has promised the one who goes out in His cause 'and does not go out except with faith in Me and for Jihad in My cause"
"5030","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Allah"
"5031","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The delegation of 'Abdul-Qais came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and said: 'We are a group of people from (the tribe of) Rabi'ah"
"5032","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Whoever follows the funeral procession of a Muslim out of faith and in the hope of reward"
"5033","It was narrated from Salim"
"5034","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Indeed"
"5035","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:The Prophet [SAW] entered upon her and there was a woman with her. He said: ""Who is this?"" She said: ""So-and-so; she does not sleep""- she mentioned her excessive praying. The Prophet [SAW] said: ""Keep quiet. You should do what you are able to"
"5036","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Soon the best wealth of a Muslim will be the sheep which follows in the mountain peaks and places where rainfall is to be found"
"5037","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that :The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""The parable of the hypocrite is that of a sheep that hesitates between two flocks"
"5038","Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari said:""The Prophet [SAW] said: 'The parable of the believer who recites the Qur'an is that of a citron"
"5039","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that:The Prophet [SAW] said: ""None of you has believed until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself"
"5040","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""Ten things are part of the Fitrah: Trimming the mustache"
"5041","Al-Mu'tamir narrated that his father said:""I heard Talq mentioning ten things that have to do with the Fitrah: Using the Siwak"
"5042","It was narrated that Talq bin Habib said:""Ten things are from the Sunnah: Using the Siwak"
"5043","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Five things are of the Fitrah: Circumcision"
"5044","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""Five things are of the Fitrah: Clipping the nails"
"5045","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar:That the Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""Trim the mustache and let the beard grow"
"5046","Ibn 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Let the beard grow and trim the mustache"
"5047","It was narrated that Zaid bin Al-Arqam said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: 'Whoever does not take from his mustache"
"5048","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that :The Prophet [SAW] saw a boy"